{
  "title": {
    "id": "title",
    "x": 400,
    "y": -2,
    "width": 800,
    "height": 60,
    "z": 1,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 60px;text-align:center",
    "text": "SORT: Introduction"
  },
  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1400,
    "height": 150,
    "layer": -3,
    "z": 1,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 25px; ",
    "html": "SORT rearranges the widgets in a holder, or in a SELECTed collection, by one or more of their properties, called <b>keys</b>. Any property can be a key. The default deck of cards has several properties useful for sorting. Deal a row, drag a few cards out of order, then use the buttons to put them back."
  },
  "button1": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button1",
    "x": 129,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "Sort by rank",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "row",
        "key": "rank"
      }
    ],
    "width": 130
  },
  "button2": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button2",
    "x": 537,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "Sort by suit, then rank",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "row",
        "key": [
          "suit",
          "rank"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "width": 220
  },
  "button3": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button3",
    "x": 953,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "Suits up, ranks down",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "row",
        "key": [
          "suit",
          {
            "key": "rank",
            "reverse": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "width": 200
  },
  "button4": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button4",
    "x": 1359,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "reverse: true",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "row",
        "key": [
          "suit",
          "rank"
        ],
        "reverse": true
      }
    ],
    "width": 140
  },
  "text1": {
    "id": "text1",
    "x": 14,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>key</b>: names the property to sort by and defaults to <i>\"value\"</i>. This deck's <i>rank</i> is zero-padded (\"02\" … \"10\", then \"2J\", \"3Q\", \"4K\"), so text order is card order and aces come first."
  },
  "text2": {
    "id": "text2",
    "x": 421,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "An array of keys sorts by the first one and breaks ties with the next: <i>[\"suit\", \"rank\"]</i> collects the suits and orders each of them by rank."
  },
  "text3": {
    "id": "text3",
    "x": 836,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "Every entry can also be an object with options of its own: <i>[\"suit\", {key: \"rank\", reverse: true}]</i> flips just that key — the suits still ascend while the ranks inside each suit descend."
  },
  "text4": {
    "id": "text4",
    "x": 1234,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>reverse</b>: flips the whole result after all keys are applied, highest card first. With several keys that is not the same as reversing each key on its own."
  },
  "row": {
    "type": "holder",
    "id": "row",
    "x": 100,
    "y": 460,
    "width": 1400,
    "height": 180,
    "dropTarget": {
      "type": "card"
    }
  },
  "text5": {
    "id": "text5",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 665,
    "width": 1400,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>holder</b>: SORTs the listed holder. In this variant, all the buttons SORT the holder directly above. You can also sort a whole list of holders at once when listed as an array. Without <b>holder</b>, SORT orders a SELECTed <b>collection</b> instead. The next variant shows that together with the other SORT properties: <b>groupBy</b>, <b>order</b>, <b>locales</b> and <b>rearrange</b>."
  },
